    skos:definition "a heavy spar or sulphate, the white varieties of which are ground and made into paint. The nitrates are used for producing a green flame; nearly all the salts are virulent poisons. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 40]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_industrial_minerals): Named mineral (slates, felspar, barytes, kieselguhr) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 1 rows, 1871–1871. Series: CSP_Canadian Trade and Navigation ×1. Units: Tons ×1. Top routes: Nova Scotia → United States ×1."@en ;
